# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# Generated voice clips.
#
# Ignored by default so a fork without a TTS key is not carrying ~11 MB of
# audio it cannot use. If you want the clips generated ONCE and then shipped
# with the repo — so every build and every install has the same voice without
# ever calling the API again — commit them deliberately:
#
#   npm run gen:voice
#   git add -f assets/voice
#
# The generator skips anything already on disk, so a later run only pays for
# words you have added since. See VOICE_SETUP.md.
assets/voice/*.mp3
# The second recorded voice, generated by `VOICE_SET=m npm run gen:voice`, on
# the same terms. It is all-or-nothing: check:voice fails on a partial set,
# because a word with no clip in the chosen voice falls through to the device's
# own text-to-speech, which has no Urdu.
assets/voice-m/*.mp3

# Voice auditions — one sample line per candidate voice, written by
# `npm run gen:voice -- --audition`. Scratch output for choosing a narrator by
# ear; never shipped, never required by the manifest.
assets/voice-audition/

